  "review": {
    "book": "JOS",
    "entityID": "place:benjamin-territory_1293",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "The lot of the tribe of the children of Benjamin came up according to their families. The border of their lot went out between the children of Judah and the children of Joseph."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Their border on the north quarter was from the Jordan. The border went up to the side of Jericho on the north, and went up through the hill country westward. It ended at the wilderness of Beth Aven."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border passed along from there to Luz, to the side of Luz (also called Bethel), southward. The border went down to Ataroth Addar, by the mountain that lies on the south of Beth Horon the lower."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border extended, and turned around on the west quarter southward, from the mountain that lies before Beth Horon southward; and ended at Kiriath Baal (also called Kiriath Jearim), a city of the children of Judah. This was the west quarter."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "The south quarter was from the farthest part of Kiriath Jearim. The border went out westward, and went out to the spring of the waters of Nephtoah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border went down to the farthest part of the mountain that lies before the valley of the son of Hinnom, which is in the valley of Rephaim northward. It went down to the valley of Hinnom, to the side of the Jebusite southward, and went down to En Rogel."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "It extended northward, went out at En Shemesh, and went out to Geliloth, which is opposite the ascent of Adummim. It went down to the stone of Bohan the son of Reuben."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "It passed along to the side opposite the Arabah northward, and went down to the Arabah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border passed along to the side of Beth Hoglah northward; and the border ended at the north bay of the Salt Sea, at the south end of the Jordan. This was the south border."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "The Jordan was its border on the east quarter. This was the inheritance of the children of Benjamin, by the borders around it, according to their families."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now the cities of the tribe of the children of Benjamin according to their families were Jericho, Beth Hoglah, Emek Keziz,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Chephar Ammoni, Ophni, and Geba; twelve cities with their villages."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "Gibeon, Ramah, Beeroth,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 18:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "Zelah, Eleph, the Jebusite (also called Jerusalem), Gibeath, and Kiriath; fourteen cities with their villages. This is the inheritance of the children of Benjamin according to their families."
      }
    ],
